  "raw": " usual amount, and the majority of fathers also took less than their higher-paid male colleagues.\n\nRead more\n\nRead More\n\nCraig Steven is director at Management in Society, a Washington, DC-based research institute that is developing a strategy to promote gender equality in its big survey taken of people who manage and work for large Fortune 500 companies.\n\nThe study, which was released Tuesday, hit on patterns familiar to any man doing the yard work or taking care of sick children in the house: that no one is taking paternity leave, men are taking less, men in more senior and high-paying jobs are taking more, men in lower-paid roles are taking less.\n\nTeens and the task of building a healthy relationship\n\nTeens and the task of building a healthy relationship\n\nReady, set, parenting is officially a thing. Newly graduated students are contacting schools in droves, desperate for tips on how to tackle the task of raising children. Columnist",
